{"sub":"Monday 23 November 2026 · GBP/USD. Watches the London killzone so you do not have to trade it: a map at 06:40, the leg and its equilibrium at 10:00, a scorecard at noon. It never calls a trade.","feed":"<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">06:40<small>Morning map</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--blue)\">Morning map</span><h2>Friday's high is already gone. The open pools are below.</h2><p class=\"lede\">Before London opens, this is where the resting orders are and how often price has gone to get them by noon.</p><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD · 1.31288</strong><span class=\"side map\">DRAW MAP</span></header><div class=\"pools\"><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Asia low<small>1.30947 · 34.1p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:18%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">18%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Friday's low<small>1.30798 · 49.0p below</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:2%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">2%</div></div><div class=\"pool\"><div class=\"nm\">Last week's high<small>1.32283 · 99.5p above</small></div><div class=\"meter\"><i style=\"--p:0%\"></i></div><div class=\"odds\">0%</div></div></div></div><p>GBP/USD ran Friday's high (1.31287) at 06:30 and printed 1.31332, so the nearest buy-side pool was spent before the session. The Asia range is still open until 07:00; its high is being made right now.</p><p>Monday is the week's manipulation day: read the run, don't trust it yet. No red news on the calendar.</p><p class=\"dim\">Watching only. Handover at 10:00.</p><section class=\"stage\" aria-label=\"Session chart\"><header><div><strong id=\"cPair\"></strong><small>15m · UK time</small></div><div class=\"views\" id=\"views\"></div></header>\n<svg class=\"chart\" id=\"chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Candlestick chart of the session with the desk's levels\"></svg><div class=\"pdk\" id=\"pdk\"></div><div class=\"scap\" id=\"cap\"></div></section></div></article>\n<article class=\"post\"><div class=\"time\">10:00<small>Handover</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--copper)\">Killzone handover</span><h2>A 29-pip leg up took the Asia high, then gave it all back.</h2><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side map\">HANDOVER</span></header><dl><dt>Leg</dt><dd><span class=\"px \">1.31171</span> at 08:00 → <span class=\"px \">1.31457</span> at 08:45 · 28.6 pips up</dd><dt>Swept</dt><dd>Asia high <span class=\"px \">1.31332</span> at 08:30, ran 12.5 pips past it</dd><dt>Equilibrium</dt><dd><span class=\"px c\">1.31314</span> · 13.7 pips above price · already crossed at 09:00</dd><dt>Price</dt><dd><span class=\"px \">1.31177</span> · back at the start of the leg</dd><dt>Still unspent</dt><dd>Asia low <span class=\"px \">1.30947</span> 23p below (33%) · Friday's low <span class=\"px \">1.30798</span> 38p below (17%)</dd></dl></div><p>London ran the buy stops above the Asia high and Friday's high, then reversed the whole move inside an hour. That is the Monday manipulation the map warned about: the buy side is spent, and every open pool now sits below.</p></div></article>","week":"<section class=\"week\"><h3>Meridian 2 · week of 23 Nov · equilibrium reached by noon</h3><div class=\"wk\"><div class=\"\"><small>Mon</small><b class=\"\">live</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Tue</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Wed</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Thu</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Fri</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"tot\"><small>Week</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div></div></section>","date":"Monday 23 November 2026","chart":{"pair":"GBP/USD","bars":[["00:00",1.30959,1.31024,1.30947,1.31022],["00:15",1.31019,1.31037,1.30988,1.31035],["00:30",1.31032,1.31047,1.31006,1.31031],["00:45",1.31026,1.31072,1.31026,1.31069],["01:00",1.31067,1.31122,1.31058,1.31103]